#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn to start the Orca screen reader, set its keyboard layout and modifier, "
"and read web pages in Firefox with keyboard commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:8
msgid "Topics: Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:12
msgid "Get started with the screen reader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:14
msgid ""
"Ubuntu Desktop comes with the Orca screen reader. Orca is an open-source "
"tool that reads text on your screen and lets you navigate the user interface "
"using keyboard commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:16
msgid ""
"Let's explore how to start the screen reader and use the Ubuntu Desktop "
"interface without relying on vision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:19
msgid "Enable the screen reader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:21
msgid ""
"First, close all windows. It's best to work on a clean desktop so that "
"certain applications don't capture your keyboard commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:23
msgid ""
"To start the screen reader, press {kbd}`Super+Alt+S`. What we call the {kbd}"
"`Super` key is the key with the Windows logo on PC keyboards, or the {kbd}"
"`Cmd` key on Apple keyboards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:25
msgid "Orca immediately announces \"screen reader on\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:27
msgid ""
"You can later turn off the screen reader using the same keyboard shortcut. "
"For now, keep it enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:30
msgid "Determine your keyboard layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:32
msgid ""
"Orca uses different keyboard commands depending on the size and layout of "
"your keyboard. Before you learn about Orca commands, you need to find out "
"which layout Orca is using."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:34
msgid ""
"Press {kbd}`Alt+F2`. The {guilabel}`Run a command` dialog opens and Orca "
"announces it. If the dialog doesn't open, you might need to press the {kbd}"
"`Fn` key with {kbd}`F2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:36
msgid "Type `orca --setup` into the dialog and press {kbd}`Enter`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:38
msgid ""
"The {guilabel}`Screen Reader Preferences` window opens. The {guilabel}"
"`Profiles` tab is active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:40
msgid ""
"Using the {kbd}`Arrow Down` key, navigate to the {guilabel}`Commands` tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:42
msgid ""
"Press {kbd}`Tab`. Focus moves to the first element in the window, which is a "
"keyboard layout selector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:44
msgid "Orca announces what your layout is: laptop or desktop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:46
msgid ""
"If you're using a laptop keyboard, make sure that the laptop layout is "
"selected. You can switch using the arrow keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:49
msgid ""
"If you set the desktop layout with a laptop keyboard, you won't be able to "
"enter Orca commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:52
msgid "For now, close the preferences window using {kbd}`Alt+F4`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:54
msgid ""
"If you've changed your keyboard layout, the app asks you to save changes. "
"Confirm by selecting {guilabel}`Save to Default and close`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:57
msgid "The Orca modifier on your keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:59
msgid ""
"Most of the keyboard commands that control Orca start with the *Orca "
"modifier*. It's a key that acts like {kbd}`Shift` or {kbd}`Ctrl`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:61
msgid "With the laptop layout, you use {kbd}`CapsLock` as your Orca modifier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:63
msgid ""
"You might encounter issues with the {kbd}`CapsLock` modifier. Sometimes, the "
"system treats it as plain {kbd}`CapsLock` when it should act as the Orca "
"modifier, or the other way around."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:65
msgid ""
"In that case, toggle {kbd}`CapsLock` by double-pressing it. Alternatively, "
"press {kbd}`CapsLock+Backspace`, which tells Orca to ignore the next key, "
"and then press {kbd}`CapsLock`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:67
msgid "With the desktop layout, it's {kbd}`Insert`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:69
msgid ""
"Make sure to disable your {kbd}`NumLock`. Many commands on the desktop "
"layout use keys on the numeric keypad, and they only work when {kbd}"
"`NumLock` is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:72
msgid "Ask for the time and date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:74
msgid "Let's try an Orca command now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:76
msgid ""
"To let Orca tell you the current time, press Orca modifier + {kbd}`T`. "
"That's {kbd}`CapsLock+T` if you have the laptop layout, or {kbd}`Insert+T` "
"on the desktop layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:78
msgid "Orca tells you the current hour, minute and second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:80
msgid ""
"To find out today's date, double-press {kbd}`T` in the same keyboard "
"shortcut. Use {kbd}`CapsLock+T+T` on the laptop layout, or {kbd}`Insert+T+T` "
"on the desktop layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:82
msgid ""
"Orca says the date only as numbers. For example, if you hear \"zero seven "
"thirty two thousand twenty five\", that represents July 30, 2025."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:85
msgid "Check your internet connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:87
msgid ""
"In the following sections, we'll cover some basic Orca controls in a web "
"browser. Before we launch the web browser, let's ensure that the internet "
"connection is on. In the process, we're going to explore how to control the "
"desktop interface from the keyboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:89
msgid ""
"Network settings are available in the top bar. Press {kbd}`Ctrl+Alt+Tab` to "
"cycle through the areas of the user interface. Notice that you can also "
"focus the Dash, which contains application launchers, and the desktop icons "
"frame. Select \"Top Bar\" and release the keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:91
msgid ""
"Now, you can browse the elements in the top bar. Press {kbd}`Tab` until you "
"hear \"System Menu\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:93
msgid ""
"Press {kbd}`Enter` to activate the menu and press {kbd}`Down` to descend "
"into the quick settings menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:95
msgid ""
"Inside the menu, you can again use {kbd}`Tab` to cycle through the menu "
"items. You'll hear items such as the battery percentage, a screenshot "
"button, a settings button, a screen lock button and a power off button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:97
msgid ""
"Eventually, you might arrive to the {guilabel}`Wired` toggle button. If Orca "
"says that the button is \"pressed\", you're connected to wired network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:99
msgid ""
"You might also encounter the {guilabel}`Wi-Fi` toggle button. If it's "
"\"pressed\", it means that the wireless subsystem is enabled. However, you "
"might not be connected to any wireless network. Let's find out:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:101
msgid "Press {kbd}`Tab` again and go to the \"Open Menu\" button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:102
msgid ""
"Activate it and press {kbd}`Down` to descend into the list of wireless "
"networks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:103
msgid ""
"If you're connected to a wireless network, it's the first one on the list. "
"Orca tells you the network name, security, the signal strength, and says "
"\"checked\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:105
msgid ""
"If you're not connected to any wireless network, Orca doesn't say "
"\"checked\". In that case, browse the network list using {kbd}`Up` and {kbd}"
"`Down`. When you find your network, activate it, and if asked, enter the "
"password."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:108
msgid "Launch Firefox"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:110
msgid ""
"Let's try opening an application and learning where we are. In this example, "
"we'll use the Firefox web browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:112
msgid "Start Firefox:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:114
msgid "Press {kbd}`Super` to open the applications overview and search."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:116
msgid ""
"Start typing _Firefox_. Type slowly letter by letter and listen to what Orca "
"says."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:118
msgid ""
"Orca announces which application currently matches the search term. When you "
"type \"f\", Firefox might already be the current match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:120
msgid ""
"When Firefox is the active search result, press {kbd}`Enter` to open Firefox."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:122
msgid "When Firefox opens, Orca says: \"Mozilla Firefox frame\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:124
msgid ""
"In Firefox, open a new tab so that we're on the same page: press {kbd}"
"`Ctrl+T`. Orca announces: \"New Tab page tab\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:126
msgid "Let's explore where we are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:128
msgid ""
"Ask for the window title. With the laptop layout, press {kbd}`CapsLock+/`. "
"With the desktop layout, press {kbd}`Insert+Enter` on the numeric keypad."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:130
msgid "Orca announces: \"Mozilla Firefox\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:132
msgid ""
"Ask about the active element in the window. Press Orca modifier + {kbd}"
"`Enter`. This is also called the *basic Where Am I*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:134
msgid ""
"Right now, the active element should be the address bar in the new tab. Orca "
"announces: \"Navigation toolbar\" and some additional details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:137
msgid ""
"You might be using multiple keyboard layouts or a different keyboard layout "
"than your interface language. In that case, Orca commands might follow a "
"different keyboard layout than expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:139
msgid ""
"If some Orca commands work and others don't, try entering them as if another "
"keyboard layout was active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:142
msgid "Read the application content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:144
msgid "Let's read some web pages. We'll start with a simple one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:146
msgid "Enter [`example.org`](https://example.org) in the Firefox address bar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:148
msgid ""
"To read the entire page content, press Orca modifier + {kbd}`;`. The page "
"contains one heading, two paragraphs and one link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:150
msgid ""
"Let's compare that with another way to read the content of applications: "
"Flat Review. To read the whole window, press Orca modifier and double-press "
"{kbd}`;`. Orca starts reading the elements of the Firefox window first "
"before it gets to the web page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:152
msgid ""
"Another common way to read text is caret navigation. Press {kbd}`F7` and "
"confirm using {kbd}`Alt+Y`. Use the arrow keys to move your text cursor "
"(caret) on the web page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:154
msgid "Pressing {kbd}`Left` and {kbd}`Right` reads the text by letter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:155
msgid "Pressing {kbd}`Ctrl+Left` and {kbd}`Ctrl+Right` reads the text by word."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:156
msgid "Pressing {kbd}`Up` and {kbd}`Down` reads the text by line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:158
msgid ""
"Try placing your cursor roughly to the middle of the document. When you "
"press Orca modifier + {kbd}`;` to read the document, it starts reading from "
"your current position to the end of the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:161
msgid "Focus elements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:163
msgid ""
"The [`example.org`](https://example.org) page contains one link. Press {kbd}"
"`Tab` to switch focus to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:165
msgid ""
"As you press {kbd}`Tab` again, the focus moves through interactive elements "
"in the Firefox interface until it cycles back to the link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:167
msgid ""
"When you focus the link, Orca tells you where the link leads. To repeat the "
"information, press Orca modifier + {kbd}`Enter`. The is the *basic Where Am "
"I* command. To hear more information, press Orca modifier and double-press "
"{kbd}`Enter`. This is the *detailed Where Am I* command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:169
msgid ""
"Press {kbd}`Enter` to activate the focused element. In this case, follow the "
"link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:172
msgid "Browsing the web using Structural Navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:174
msgid ""
"We've opened a longer, more complex web page: [Example Domains](https://"
"www.iana.org/help/example-domains)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:176
msgid ""
"If you press Orca modifier + {kbd}`;` to hear the whole page, you'll notice "
"that you might not be interested in every part. Press {kbd}`Escape` to stop "
"reading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:178
msgid ""
"With Structural Navigation, you can read the page by headings, links, lists "
"and other elements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:180
msgid "To get a list of **headings** on this page, press {kbd}`Alt+Shift+H`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:182
msgid "Move through the headings using {kbd}`H` and {kbd}`Shift+H`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:184
msgid "To get a list of **links** on this page, press {kbd}`Alt+Shift+K`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:186
msgid "Move through the links using {kbd}`K` and {kbd}`Shift+K`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:188
msgid "To get a list of **lists** on this page, press {kbd}`Alt+Shift+L`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:190
msgid "Move through the lists using {kbd}`L` and {kbd}`Shift+L`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:192
msgid "To get a list of **paragraphs** on this page, press {kbd}`Alt+Shift+P`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:194
msgid "Move through the paragraphs using {kbd}`P` and {kbd}`Shift+P`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:196
msgid ""
"Orca supports many more Structural Navigation commands. You can find a "
"complete reference at {ref}`orca-structural-navigation-commands`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:199
msgid ""
"If a form field or another kind of text entry is focused, Structural "
"Navigation commands don't work because you're typing text. To re-enable "
"Structural Navigation, press Orca modifier + {kbd}`Z`. Alternatively, leave "
"the field using {kbd}`Tab`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:203
msgid "Other applications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:205
msgid ""
"In other applications, you can use most of the commands that we've covered:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:207
msgid "Usually, you want to use {kbd}`Tab` to browse the interactive elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:209
msgid ""
"In text editors, caret navigation works by default. In some other "
"applications like document viewers, you can enable it using {kbd}`F7`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:211
msgid ""
"Try using the commands to read the document and read the window: Orca "
"modifier + {kbd}`;` and Orca modifier + {kbd}`;+;`. In some applications, "
"such as text editors and other text entries, the commands might not work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:213
msgid ""
"Only a couple of application support Structural Navigation: Firefox, "
"LibreOffice, Thunderbird and Pidgin. In LibreOffice, you can only use "
"Structural navigation to browse tables in Writer. In editable documents, "
"enable Structural navigation using Orca modifier + {kbd}`Z`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:215
msgid ""
"If you experience difficulty with some applications, you can find tips in "
"{ref}`Improve screen reader usability <improve-screen-reader-usability>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:218
msgid "Learn more"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:220
msgid ""
"Orca has a learning mode where keys and commands only tell you what their "
"function is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:222
msgid ""
"To enter learning mode, press Orca modifier + {kbd}`H`. Try various Orca "
"commands that you remember. Try pressing other keys with your Orca modifier. "
"Each time, Orca tells you what the command does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:224
msgid ""
"Press {kbd}`F2` to open a list of Orca keyboard commands. You can browse the "
"list using {kbd}`Up` and {kbd}`Down`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:226
msgid "To exit learning mode, press {kbd}`Escape`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:228
msgid "For more guidance, go to the following pages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:230
msgid "{ref}`navigate-the-screen-using-the-screen-reader`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:231
msgid "{ref}`read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:232
msgid "{ref}`read-screen-in-braille`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:233
msgid "{ref}`navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:234
msgid "{ref}`keyboard-navigation-shortcuts`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/get-started-with-the-screen-reader.md:235
msgid "{ref}`improve-screen-reader-usability`"
msgstr ""
